# ============================================================
# Beads .gitignore — canonical for cosalette
# ============================================================
# SOURCE OF TRUTH: the Dolt database in .beads/dolt/. It is
# exchanged with the team over the Dolt remote (`bd dolt push` /
# `bd dolt pull`, i.e. `task beads:push` / `task beads:pull`,
# against the GitHub origin under refs/dolt/*) — NOT via any
# committed file.
#
# TRACKED (committed to git):
#   config.yaml      — team-wide beads configuration
#   metadata.json    — project identity (database name, backend)
#   hooks/           — git hook scripts managed by beads
#   README.md        — documentation
#   .gitignore       — this file
#
# NOT TRACKED — issues.jsonl:
#   `bd export` / `task beads:sync` writes .beads/issues.jsonl as
#   a LOCAL-ONLY snapshot for inspection and diffing. It is
#   gitignored and untracked since the 2026-08 security audit
#   (F-SC1 / CWE-359: the export embeds a maintainer's personal
#   email in ~655 places). It is ignored TWICE, deliberately:
#     1. the ROOT .gitignore (unanchored `issues.jsonl`), and
#     2. `/issues.jsonl` in this file — the first rule below.
#   Either layer alone is sufficient, so BOTH must stay: dropping
#   one cannot silently re-expose the export. Do not weaken either,
#   and never `git add .beads/issues.jsonl`.
#
# EVERYTHING ELSE is ephemeral / machine-local and must NOT
# be committed.
# ============================================================

# ── Local-only issue export — SECOND ignore layer (F-SC1) ─────
# Deliberate duplicate of the root .gitignore rule. It is NOT
# redundant: it keeps .beads/issues.jsonl out of git even if the
# root rule is ever removed. Anchored so it matches this directory's
# issues.jsonl only, never a nested path.
/issues.jsonl

# ── Dolt database (per-machine; replicated via the Dolt remote) ─
dolt/

# ── Legacy embedded Dolt (removed in bd ≥1.0) ─────────────────
embeddeddolt/

# ── Backup directories (auto-generated, contain .darc blobs) ──
backup/
backup.bak/

# ── Dolt server runtime ───────────────────────────────────────
dolt-server.pid
dolt-server.log
dolt-server.lock
dolt-server.port
dolt-server.activity

# ── Beads runtime state ───────────────────────────────────────
bd.sock
bd.sock.startlock
sync-state.json
push-state.json
last-touched
interactions.jsonl
.exclusive-lock
.local_version

# ── Daemon artifacts (legacy, removed in bd ≥0.50) ────────────
daemon.*

# ── Lock files ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.lock

# ── Credential key (encryption key — NEVER commit) ────────────
.beads-credential-key

# ── Worktree redirect (machine-specific path) ─────────────────
redirect

# ── Sync/export state (per-machine) ──────────────────────────
.sync.lock
export-state/
export-state.json
last_pull

# ── Proxied Dolt server runtime (per-machine) ────────────────
proxieddb/
proxied_server_client_info.json

# ── Ephemeral store (wisps/molecules, not versioned) ──────────
ephemeral.sqlite3
ephemeral.sqlite3-journal
ephemeral.sqlite3-wal
ephemeral.sqlite3-shm

# ── Corrupt backup recovery dirs ─────────────────────────────
*.corrupt.backup/

# ── Per-project env file ──────────────────────────────────────
.env

# ── Legacy SQLite databases (pre-Dolt versions) ──────────────
*.db
*.db?*
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
db.sqlite
bd.db
